<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Negative Numbers: Students often confuse "Sign and Magnitude" with "Two's Complement."</li>
        <li>K-Map Headings: Forgetting that Gray Code (00, 01, 11, 10) is mandatory for headings to ensure only one bit changes at a time.</li>
        <li>XOR Logic: Mistaking XOR for a standard OR gate (XOR is strictly "one or the other, but not both").</li>
        <li>Interrupts: Believing an interrupt is an "error" rather than a routine hardware signal for CPU attention.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

